  The effect of enchantment on missile survival is capped at 75%.
Blessing is what makes them last with high luck.   Using non-blessed +0
darts twice will lose 90% of them.

  As you point out, once they stop vanishing Expert darts are the ideal
ranged weapon.  As you also point out, that's only reliably possible by
the midgame, by which time the need shouldn't be nearly as great.

  Having to wait until midgame to develop dart skill is a major
drawback.  Ranged attacks are a critical survival tactic in the early
game.  

  In the early game daggers beat darts based solely on missile survival,
despite weighing ten times as much.  So early Expert daggers beat early
Expert darts.  Every class that can get to Expert with darts can also
get to Expert with daggers.  

  Except healers, but Skilled daggers early are still well worth it.
Switching to darts at mid-game, for any class, is problematical due to
the 11 skill slots needed to get both weapons to Expert.







